    "body": "## Summary\n\n`ao browser tabs --json` returns each tab's title and URL verbatim. For signed SSO/handoff links, this emits the full query string\u2014including opaque one-time or credential-like parameters\u2014into agent tool output and retained transcripts. When a page uses the URL as its title, the secret-bearing URL is duplicated.\n\n**Reported by:** external AO user; report relayed by the project operator (public handle/source URL not supplied)  \n**Observed:** 2026-08-31 on an authenticated government portal; all secret values are intentionally omitted  \n**Analyzed against:** `main` at `ab17197b0d1bdc8d4d9849ef46675e067fc77119`  \n**Confidence:** High. Current source returns raw values.\n\n## Sanitized reproduction\n\n1. Open a page whose URL resembles:\n   `https://example.test/access?param1=<opaque>&param2=<opaque>&param3=<opaque>`\n2. Make the page title equal to that URL (the observed site did this).\n3. Run `ao browser tabs --json`.\n4. Observe the complete URL and query values in both `tabs[].url` and `tabs[].title`.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`frontend/src/main/browser-view-host.ts` builds tab results directly from:\n\n- `entry.view.webContents.getURL()`\n- `entry.view.webContents.getTitle()`\n\nThere is no output-boundary sanitization. The same file already has `sanitizeNetworkURL`, which strips credentials/fragments and redacts query values for captured network metadata, but tab results do not use an equivalent policy.\n\n## Impact\n\n- Signed handoff/SSO material is copied into agent transcripts and diagnostic logs.\n- A URL-shaped title duplicates the exposure.\n- Long opaque URLs can exhaust tool-output budgets.\n\nNo matching open or closed issue was found for browser-tab URL redaction.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- Default tab output is safe to retain: preserve origin/path while redacting query values, credentials, and fragments.\n- Sanitize URL-shaped titles as well as `url`.\n- Apply the policy at the trusted Electron/daemon response boundary so text and JSON output are both protected.\n- Keep an explicit, clearly unsafe opt-in only if full URL retrieval is genuinely required.\n- Cover ordinary URLs, query strings, fragments, embedded credentials, URL-shaped titles, opaque/high-entropy values, and malformed URLs.\n- Audit browser errors and other tab metadata paths for the same raw-URL exposure.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-01T16:25:33Z",
